{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790714409,"nonce":"RlK+sZDnA6kOAFE2Zf3hHoshCyk=","title":"Capture sketch thumbnails on save","message":"\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Defines thumbnail capture and preservation for saved desktop sketches. --\u003e\n\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Specifies current-preview capture without rerunning source or corrupting saved images. --\u003e\n\n# Capture sketch thumbnails on save\n\n## Parent\n\n02e51b7 / https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/84\n\n## What to build\n\nOn desktop Save and Save As, persist a PNG captured from the currently displayed successful Canvas preview at native resolution, without rerunning the sketch. Source and description saves remain available when source is broken or a preview is unavailable; in those cases, never replace an existing saved thumbnail. Ensure captures cannot cross documents or use stale preview results. Preserve unrelated files. This slice extends the desktop save behavior in stories 9–10 and delivers stories 14–17.\n\nUser stories: 14–17; extends stories 9–10.\n\nRelated context only: broad requests 948a98c and 0ac47e5. This slice does not replace, close, or modify those issues.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Desktop Save captures the currently displayed successful Canvas preview at its native pixel dimensions, with no resize or crop and no additional execution of GIC. Preserve once-only format-on-save behavior; capture does not trigger another language execution.\n- [ ] Save As applies the same capture rule to the copy while preserving the source sketch and its files.\n- [ ] A broken or invalid source remains saveable. If preview execution fails, times out, is unavailable, or has been cleared, source and description saving can still succeed and an existing saved thumbnail remains unchanged.\n- [ ] A thumbnail is accepted only for the active sketch's current successful preview; stale worker results, a superseded preview, or another document's Canvas cannot be captured.\n- [ ] A failed or cancelled save is not reported as completed, and unrelated files and existing bundle contents remain intact.\n- [ ] Automated desktop integration tests use real temporary files and real PNG data. Verify PNG persistence, preservation of an existing thumbnail when preview capture is unavailable, Save As, and unrelated-file preservation. Do not use these native file tests as evidence of displayed Canvas pixels or execution count, and do not mock file operations.\n- [ ] Automated shared Playwright tests drive the real editor, worker, and Canvas to verify successful-preview freshness and source/document isolation at the existing capture seam. They verify capture/freshness only, not native PNG persistence, Canvas-to-file pixel equivalence, or no-rerun behavior; do not add hidden DOM state or a test-only bridge.\n- [ ] Packaged macOS acceptance exercises desktop Save and Save As with a real preview, compares saved PNG dimensions and visible pixels with the actual displayed Canvas, and uses a random sketch to prove saving does not rerun GIC. Confirm once-only format-on-save, and that broken source or unavailable preview leaves an existing thumbnail intact.\n\n## Blocked by\n\ngit-bug `e132361` — Author, save, and reopen sketch descriptions.","files":null}]}